<tool id="hicexplorer_chicchicagosignificantinteractions" name="@BINARY@" version="@TOOL_VERSION@+galaxy@VERSION_SUFFIX@" profile="@PROFILE@">
    <description>selects significant CHiCAGO interactions</description>
    <macros>
        <token name="@BINARY@">chicChicagoSignificantInteractions</token>
        <import>macros.xml</import>
    </macros>
    <expand macro="requirements" />
    <command detect_errors="exit_code"><![CDATA[
        @BINARY@

            --scores '$scores'
            --rmap '$rmap'
            --baitmap '$baitmap'
            --outFileName significant_interactions.txt

            --scoreThreshold $scoreThreshold
            --threads @THREADS@
]]>
    </command>
    <inputs>
        <param argument="--scores" type="data" format="tabular,txt" label="CHiCAGO scores" help="chicChicagoScores' own output file." />
        <param argument="--rmap" type="data" format="tabular,txt" label="CHiCAGO .rmap file" />
        <param argument="--baitmap" type="data" format="tabular,txt" label="CHiCAGO .baitmap file" />
        <param argument="--scoreThreshold" type="float" value="5.0" label="Minimum CHiCAGO score to call an interaction significant" />
    </inputs>
    <outputs>
        <data name="outFileName" from_work_dir="significant_interactions.txt" format="tabular" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: Significant interactions" />
    </outputs>
    <tests>
        <test expect_num_outputs="1">
            <param name="scores" value="chicChicago/scores.txt" ftype="tabular" />
            <param name="rmap" value="chicChicago/h19_min.rmap" ftype="tabular" />
            <param name="baitmap" value="chicChicago/h19_min.baitmap" ftype="tabular" />
            <output name="outFileName" ftype="tabular">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_line line="bait_chr&#009;bait_start&#009;bait_end&#009;bait_name&#009;otherEnd_chr&#009;otherEnd_start&#009;otherEnd_end&#009;N&#009;distSign&#009;score" />
                    <has_n_columns n="10" />
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <test expect_num_outputs="1">
            <param name="scores" value="chicChicago/scores.txt" ftype="txt" />
            <param name="rmap" value="chicChicago/h19_min.rmap" ftype="txt" />
            <param name="baitmap" value="chicChicago/h19_min.baitmap" ftype="txt" />
            <param name="scoreThreshold" value="2.0" />
            <output name="outFileName" ftype="tabular">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_line line="bait_chr&#009;bait_start&#009;bait_end&#009;bait_name&#009;otherEnd_chr&#009;otherEnd_start&#009;otherEnd_end&#009;N&#009;distSign&#009;score" />
                    <has_n_columns n="10" />
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
    </tests>
    <help><![CDATA[

CHiCAGO significant interactions
==================================

**chicChicagoSignificantInteractions** selects the bait-other end pairs from ``chicChicagoScores``' own output whose CHiCAGO score clears a threshold.

New in HiCExplorer v4: a native C++ implementation of CHiCAGO's own statistical model (Cairns et al. 2016), not an invented stand-in.

_________________

Output
------

The output keeps only the rows of the scores file at or above *Minimum CHiCAGO score*, in CHiCAGO's own score file format. CHiCAGO's own convention treats 5 as its standard significance threshold.

_________________

For more information about HiCExplorer please consider our documentation on readthedocs.io_.

.. _readthedocs.io: http://hicexplorer.readthedocs.io/en/latest/index.html

]]>    </help>
    <expand macro="citations">
        <citation type="doi">10.1186/s13059-016-0992-y</citation>
    </expand>
</tool>
